<!--
  ============================================================================
  BuzzerApostrophe_Fix.xml                   Jawa_Patches · authored 2026-08-14
  ============================================================================

  THE GOAL
  ========
  Det's Xenotypes - Buzzers generates faction and settlement names that can
  carry a DOUBLED apostrophe, and can never carry none. Two rule strings, one
  character each. Smoking gun from the last world: the settlement `Caz'vi''vi`.

  WHY IT IS BROKEN  [MEASURED 2026-08-14, from the mod's own XML, game down]
  ==========================================================================
  Source of truth, read directly:

    .../workshop/content/294100/3545293786/1.6/Defs/RulePackDefs/
      RulePacks_Namers_Faction.xml
        line 16  DV_NamerFactionOutlanderBuzzer
        line 56  DV_NamerSettlementOutlanderBuzzer

      <li>maybeApostrophe->''</li>        the defect
      <li>maybeApostrophe(p=3)->'</li>    fine as written

  The author wanted a "sometimes an apostrophe" symbol. In RimWorld's grammar an
  EMPTY production is written with nothing after the arrow. Writing `''`
  instead does not mean "empty string" — the grammar has no quoting, so those
  are TWO LITERAL APOSTROPHES.

  THE ARITHMETIC, because the filed figure deserved its derivation
  ===============================================================
  Default weight is 1; the second rule declares p=3. Total 4.

      25%  ->  ''   two apostrophes     (intended: none)
      75%  ->  '    one apostrophe

  So the "no apostrophe" branch became a "double apostrophe" branch, and a
  Buzzer name NEVER comes out clean. `nameCore` chains up to TWO of these, so a
  single name can draw the doubled branch twice.

  ⭐ THE AUTHOR WAS COPYING A VANILLA IDIOM AND MISSED ONE CHARACTER
  =================================================================
  Vanilla writes exactly this shape, empty RHS and all:

      <li>maybeHyphen(p=3)-></li>        Core
      <li>maybeThe-></li>                Core
      <li>skillAdvMaybe-></li>           Core

  Swept the whole `Data/` tree: 7 `questDescription->`, 3 `skillAdvMaybe->`,
  2 `maybeThe->`, 2 `maybeHyphen(p=3)->` and more. The empty production is
  ordinary, supported and idiomatic. This patch writes the same form.

  ❌ TWO CORRECTIONS TO THE FILED FINDING, both mine to make
  ==========================================================
  1. It said "vanilla leaves the right-hand side empty" for this symbol.
     **There is no vanilla `maybeApostrophe` at all** — zero hits across the
     entire `Data/` tree. The symbol is this mod's own invention, so the fix is
     justified by the vanilla IDIOM, not by a vanilla counterpart.
  2. It described ONE site. There are **TWO**: faction names and settlement
     names. Fixing one would have left half the defect in place and looked
     like the patch had failed.

  Also swept the whole workshop tree for `maybeApostrophe->''`: **exactly one
  file, this one.** It has not spread, so one patch is the whole job.

  WHAT THIS FIXES, AND WHAT IT CANNOT
  ===================================
  🔴 **Names already generated are BAKED INTO THE SAVE as plain strings.** This
  patch changes names generated in FUTURE worlds only. It is therefore worth
  shipping only while a world regeneration is still ahead of us — which it is,
  worldgen being held rather than done. After the campaign world is made, this
  patch stops being worth anything and should be judged again.

  After the fix the weights are unchanged, so: 25% no apostrophe, 75% one,
  0% doubled. The author's taste is left alone; only the broken branch moves.

  SUCCESS LOOKS LIKE
  ==================
  POSITIVE observation at the next worldgen: Buzzer faction and settlement
  names containing at most ONE apostrophe, and some containing none. There is
  no log line for this either way — a rulepack that resolves is silent.
-->
<Patch>

  <Operation Class="PatchOperationFindMod">
    <mods>
      <li>Det's Xenotypes - Buzzers</li>
    </mods>
    <match Class="PatchOperationSequence">
      <operations>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/RulePackDef[defName="DV_NamerFactionOutlanderBuzzer"]/rulePack/rulesStrings/li[text()="maybeApostrophe->''"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>maybeApostrophe-></li>
          </value>
        </li>

        <li Class="PatchOperationReplace">
          <xpath>/Defs/RulePackDef[defName="DV_NamerSettlementOutlanderBuzzer"]/rulePack/rulesStrings/li[text()="maybeApostrophe->''"]</xpath>
          <value>
            <li>maybeApostrophe-></li>
          </value>
        </li>

      </operations>
    </match>
  </Operation>

</Patch>
